From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:52:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/99] v8: e2k: pass C parameters by position, clean up C
 results

A C function takes parameter i from register i of its window whatever
the type, and the ninth and further ones from the stack. The linkage of
C calls now gives a parameter the register of its position (a<i> or
f<i>), and the call takes it from there by a mask of the floating point
ones; counting integer and floating point parameters separately, as on
loong64, passed mixed signatures wrong (fast API calls).

The result goes through memory by a speculative store: a function that
returns nothing may leave a diagnostic value in the result register, and
that would trap as soon as generated code saved its registers.

The C++ compiler leaves a 32-bit result zero-extended, the code
generator expects it sign-extended: -1 and -2 from the regexp
interpreter were taken for a match. Narrow results of calls made by
TurboFan are extended by the declared type.

Also adds TailCallC for builtins that are entered as C functions.
